   "title": "President Lee says Korea should learn from European protests to sustain growth",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/politics/20261027/president-lee-says-korea-should-learn-from-european-protests-to-sustain-growth",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:27:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793078823.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "President Lee Jae Myung said Tuesday that Korea should learn from growing public protests in Europe, citing low growth as a potential reason for the unrest and stressing the importance of ensuring sustained growth at home. The president made the remarks at a Cabinet meeting, as a wave of protests and mass demonstrations over rising living costs and economic inequality has swept across European nations, including France, Spain and Italy.",
   "summary_zh": "李在明总统周二表示，韩国应从欧洲不断扩大的公众抗议中汲取教训，并指出经济增长乏力可能是引发骚乱的原因之一，同时强调确保国内持续增长的重要性。在欧洲多国因生活成本上涨和经济不平等而爆发抗议及大规模示威之际，总统在内阁会议上发表了上述言论。欧洲发生抗议的国家包括法国、西班牙和意大利。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "President Lee Jae Myung said Tuesday that Korea should learn from growing public protests in Europe, citing low growth as a potential reason for the unrest and stressing the importance of ensuring sustained growth at home. The president made the remarks at a Cabinet meeting, as a wave of protests and mass demonstrations over rising living costs and economic inequality has swept across European nations, including France, Spain and Italy. \"As large-scale protests have occurred recently in many European countries, social confusion and conflict have ensued,\" Lee said. \"We should take the European situation as an example of what not to do.\" \"Prolonged low growth has worsened youth unemployment and (economic) polarization and weakened fiscal status, shaking social stability from the root,\" the president said of the European situation. Despite recent \"impressive results\" in Korea's economic indicators, the country is also experiencing difficulties in people's livelihoods and gaps in income, assets and jobs, especially among younger generations, Lee said. \"To solve problems like these, sustainable growth would be very important,\" he noted, instructing officials to proactively mobilize policy measures to invest in the growth of future industries, promote domestic consumption and improve people's livelihoods. Those measures would help expand the economy and stabilize state finances, laying the foundation for sustainable growth, the president said. The president also defended the attendance of the chief of the newly launched Serious Crime Investigation Agency (SCIA) at Cabinet meetings amid criticism that such attendance could compromise the agency chief's political neutrality. SCIA chief Kim Ji-yong attended Tuesday's Cabinet meeting for the second time, following his attendance at last week's meeting, breaking with the past practice of investigation agency chiefs staying away from Cabinet meetings",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "eu"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "eco"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
