   "title": "Education expert calls for teacher training to bridge gaps",
   "url": "https://dailytrust.com/education-expert-calls-for-teacher-training-to-bridge-gaps/",
   "domain": "dailytrust.com",
   "source": "Daily Trust（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:26:01 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793078761.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "The Federal Capital Territory (FCT) Secondary Education Board Desk Officer for Robotic Education, Aishatu Jafaar Suleiman, has called for extensive teachers’ training and retraining to bridge the educational gaps between teachers and students in the FCT. According to her, “The government is doing its best, and there has been so much improvement in the renovation of schools and the provision of learning materials, but teachers are in dire need of training.",
   "summary_zh": "联邦首都 Territory（FCT）中等教育委员会机器人教育事务负责人艾莎图·贾法尔·苏莱曼呼吁大力开展教师培训和再培训，以缩小FCT教师与学生之间的教育差距。据她表示：“政府正在尽最大努力，学校翻新和学习资料配备也取得了很大改善，但教师迫切需要培训。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Federal Capital Territory (FCT) Secondary Education Board Desk Officer for Robotic Education, Aishatu Jafaar Suleiman, has called for extensive teachers’ training and retraining to bridge the educational gaps between teachers and students in the FCT. Sulaiman spoke in Abuja on Monday during a sensitisation programme organised by Change a Child Community Initiative, at the Government Day Secondary School, Dutse Alhaji and Government Secondary School, Kubwa, in the Bwari Area Council. She said the administration of the FCT Minister, Nyesom Wike, is doing its best in terms of renovation of schools, provision of materials and infrastructure, but more needs to be done in teachers’ development. According to her, “The government is doing its best, and there has been so much improvement in the renovation of schools and the provision of learning materials, but teachers are in dire need of training. “We are not asking for too much, but for training and retraining so that we can give our best. “Despite not being in the class at the moment, I still train and pay for online courses that I believe will be beneficial to my profession because once a teacher, you’re always a teacher,” she said. Similarly, Founder and Lead Educator, Change a Child Community Initiative, Blessing Okwuchukwu Awamba, said the Initiative was birthed with the mindset of catching school children young and inculcating values that are needed for national development as the vices in society have continued to surge. She disclosed that the programme, which is set to run for five years, has been designed for expansion to various states, with a few states already in the kitty as beneficiaries. She said the themes, which are all-encompassing, have been well thought of and carefully selected to tally with the socioeconomic challenges being experienced within the particular geographical locations. Join Daily Trust WhatsApp Community For Quick Access To News and Happenings Around You",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "cor",
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_dailytrust",
   "title_zh": "教育专家呼吁加强教师培训，以弥补教育差距",
   "body_zh": "联邦首都领地（FCT）中等教育委员会机器人教育科干事Aishatu Jafaar Suleiman呼吁大力开展教师培训与再培训，以弥合联邦首都领地教师与学生之间的教育差距。苏莱曼周一在阿布贾出席了一场宣传活动，该活动由Change a Child Community Initiative组织，地点设在Bwari区议会管辖的Dutse Alhaji政府日间中学和Kubwa政府中学。她表示，联邦首都领地部长Nyesom Wike领导的政府正在翻新学校、提供物资和基础设施方面尽力，但教师培养方面仍有更多工作需要完成。据她介绍，“政府正在尽力而为，学校翻新和学习物资供应方面已经取得了很大改善，但教师迫切需要培训。我们提出的要求并不过分，只是希望接受培训和再培训，以便我们能够发挥最佳水平。尽管目前不在课堂上，我仍然自费参加网络课程，因为我相信这些课程对我的职业会有所裨益；因为一旦成为教师，你永远是教师。”她说。Change a Child Community Initiative创始人兼首席教育顾问Blessing Okwuchukwu Awamba表示，该倡议的宗旨是尽早接触学龄儿童，向他们灌输国家发展所需的价值观，因为社会弊端仍在不断加剧。她透露，该项目计划实施五年，并已设计为向多个州扩展，目前已有几个州被列为受益者。她说，这些涵盖各个领域的主题经过深入思考和谨慎选择，旨在与各具体地理区域所面临的社会经济挑战相适应。加入Daily Trust WhatsApp社区，快速获取身边的新闻与动态",
   "snippet_zh": ""
